{
  "_doc": "Shipped default. prefer (cheap|balanced|best) caps the tier workers may use (1|2|3; spawn --allow-tier overrides). Workers load no user MCP servers (Claude --strict-mcp-config, Codex -c mcp_servers={}). Override any part in ~/.hauptling/models.json (deep-merged). tier: 1 cheap, 2 mid, 3 top. Prices are USD per million tokens; null means unknown (cost shows as unknown). Codex keeps its workspace-write sandbox (network on so it reaches the broker); it cannot write .git, so hauptling commits for it on report/test request. Workers run in disposable containers with an egress allowlist; the container is the sandbox (Codex's own bubblewrap sandbox cannot run inside Docker, so Codex uses danger-full-access there, chosen 2026-11-21).",
  "prefer": "best",
  "rules": {
    "easy": 1,
    "normal": 2,
    "hard": 3
  },
  "order": [
    "claude",
    "codex",
    "agy"
  ],
  "vendors": {
    "claude": {
      "enabled": true,
      "launch": [
        "claude",
        "--model",
        "{model}",
        "--permission-mode",
        "auto",
        "--strict-mcp-config",
        "{prompt}"
      ],
